    {
      "id": "a6f7aac6e7eb2f80070ad7fb1207e74adba387cf02a4cd465f3c941656eba1c1",
      "name": "lodash vulnerable to Prototype Pollution via array path bypass in `_.unset` and `_.omit`",
      "description": "Lodash versions 4.17.23 and earlier are vulnerable to prototype pollution in the `_.unset` and `_.omit` functions. The fix for [CVE-2025-13465](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/security/advisories/GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg) only guards against string key members, so an attacker can bypass the check by passing array-wrapped path segments. This allows deletion of properties from built-in prototypes such as `Object.prototype`, `Number.prototype`, and `String.prototype`.\n\nThe issue permits deletion of prototype properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.",
      "severity": "Medium",
      "solution": "Upgrade to version 4.18.0 or above.",
      "location": {
        "file": "package-lock.json",
        "dependency": {
          "package": {
            "name": "lodash"
          },
          "version": "4.17.15"
        }
